<urn:atm:triage:finding/AJ-FINAL-012-DISPATCHER-CTOR-DUPLICATION>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AJ-FINAL-012-DISPATCHER-CTOR-DUPLICATION" ;
  triage:title "DaemonRequestDispatcher::new and new_for_test duplicate ~60 lines of coordinator/queue wiring with a behavioral divergence already present" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs's DaemonRequestDispatcher::new (~line 337) and new_for_test (~line 489) duplicate roughly 60 lines of coordinator/queue wiring, with one divergence already present: new_for_test eagerly calls post_commit_signals.start(), while new() defers to start_peer_drain_coordinator(). This is a drift risk -- future changes to one constructor's wiring are not mechanically guaranteed to reach the other. Found by rust-best-practices-agent during Phase AJ's final holistic gate review. QA source: PR #759." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AJ" ;
